/-!
# Change of base for the big crystalline site

Let `(S, I, γ) ⟶ (S', I', γ')` be a morphism of divided power schemes and let `X ⟶ Y` be a
morphism of schemes over the closed fibres `S₀ = V(I)` and `S'₀ = V(I')`.  A divided power
thickening `U ↪ T` of `X` relative to `(S, I, γ)` is also one of `Y` relative to `(S', I', γ')`,
with structure maps `T ⟶ S ⟶ S'` and `U ⟶ X ⟶ Y`; this is a functor
`CRIS(X/S) ⥤ CRIS(Y/S')` which is the identity on the underlying thickening.

Since the functor leaves the underlying thickening untouched, a Cartesian Zariski covering family
over the ambient scheme of an object is the same family on both sides: a Zariski covering family
of the image of `A` is `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.rebase`d to a Zariski
covering family of `A` itself, and the covering sieve it generates pulls back into the sieve
generated by the original family.

This functor is cocontinuous: a covering sieve of an object `B` of `CRIS(Y/S')` pulled back
along a morphism `p` out of the image of `A` is refined by the restrictions of `A` to the opens
`p⁻¹(Tᵢ)` of its ambient scheme, where `{Tᵢ ⟶ T_B}` is a Zariski covering family refining the
sieve; each such restriction maps into `(Uᵢ, Tᵢ, δᵢ)` because an open immersion of divided power
thickenings which is Cartesian identifies the divided power ideal of its source with the
restriction of the one of its target.  Hence change of base induces a morphism of crystalline
topoi `(X/S)_CRIS ⟶ (Y/S')_CRIS`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.ofSquare` — the object of `CRIS(X/S)` over
  `A` determined by a divided power thickening mapping to the thickening of `A`, together with
  its structure morphism `Thickening.ofSquareHom`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.restrictOpen` — the restriction of an object
  of `CRIS(X/S)` to an open of its ambient scheme, with its structure morphism
  `Thickening.restrictOpenHom` and the family `Thickening.restrictOpenCover`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.changeBase` — the functor
  `CRIS(X/S) ⥤ CRIS(Y/S')` of [Stacks, Tag 07IC].
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.rebase` — a family of morphisms into the
  image of `A`, read as a family of morphisms into `A`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.pullbackLiftHom` — the factorization of a
  morphism `r : D ⟶ C` through an open immersion `q : B ⟶ C` of `CRIS(X/S)`, over the open of the
  ambient scheme of `D` on which it exists.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.changeBaseMorphism` — the morphism of crystalline topoi
  `(X/S)_CRIS ⟶ (Y/S')_CRIS` of [Stacks, Tag 07IC].

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.isCocontinuous_toGrothendieck` — a functor into a site whose topology
  is generated by a precoverage is cocontinuous as soon as every covering presieve of the
  precoverage, pulled back along an arbitrary morphism out of the image and then along the
  functor, is covering.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover` — the
  restrictions of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to a family of opens covering its ambient scheme form
  a Zariski covering family.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isDPMorphism_appIso_inv` — for a Cartesian
  morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` which is an open immersion on ambient schemes, the inverse of the
  comparison isomorphism on sections is a morphism of divided power rings.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.changeBase_functorPullback_mem_topology` — a covering
  sieve of the image of `A` which is refined by a Zariski covering family pulls back to a
  covering sieve of `A`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.changeBase_isCocontinuous` — change of base is
  cocontinuous for the big crystalline Zariski topologies, [Stacks, Tag 07IC].

## Implementation notes

An object of `CRIS(X/S)` over a fixed `A` is the same thing as a divided power thickening
together with a morphism of thickenings into that of `A`, and `Thickening.ofSquare` is that
dictionary; it is what turns a covering family of the image of `A` into one of `A`, because
`changeBase` changes neither the thickening nor the maps between thickenings.

The cover-lifting condition quantifies over covering sieves obtained from covering families of
*other* objects by pullback, so some base change is unavoidable.  Here all the needed base
changes are along the members of a Zariski covering family, which are open immersions on ambient
schemes, and these are provided by `Crystalline.SchemeThickening.restrict` rather than by the
base change stability of the Zariski covering families, [Stacks, Tag 07IA], which is not
available.  That the restriction maps into the member it comes from is the only nonformal point:
it needs the divided power ideal of a Cartesian open immersion to be the restriction of the one
below it, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ker_ideal_of_isPullback_of_isOpenImmersion` on
affine opens and the locality of the ideal subsheaf in general.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IB)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂ u

namespace CategoryTheory.Functor

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D]

/-- **A criterion for cocontinuity into a topology generated by a precoverage.**  A functor
`u : C ⥤ D` is cocontinuous for `J` and the topology generated by a precoverage `K` as soon as,
for every covering presieve `R` of `K` and every morphism `p` out of an object of the image of
`u`, the sieve generated by `R` pulls back along `p` and then along `u` to a `J`-covering sieve.
-/
theorem isCocontinuous_toGrothendieck (u : C ⥤ D) (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    (K : Precoverage D)
    (hu : ∀ (A : C) ⦃X : D⦄ (p : u.obj A ⟶ X) (R : Presieve X), R ∈ K X →
      ((Sieve.generate R).pullback p).functorPullback u ∈ J A) :
    u.IsCocontinuous J K.toGrothendieck := by
  constructor
  intro A T hT
  suffices H : ∀ ⦃X : D⦄ (T : Sieve X), K.Saturate X T →
      ∀ (A : C) (p : u.obj A ⟶ X), (T.pullback p).functorPullback u ∈ J A by
    simpa using H _ hT A (𝟙 _)
  intro X T hT
  induction hT with
  | of X R hR => exact fun A p ↦ hu A p R hR
  | top X => intro A p; simp
  | pullback X T hT Y q ih =>
      intro A p
      rw [← Sieve.pullback_comp]
      exact ih A (p ≫ q)
  | transitive X T R hT hR ihT ihR =>
      intro A p
      refine J.transitive (ihT A p) _ ?_
      intro W k hk
      have h2 := ihR hk W (𝟙 _)
      rw [Sieve.pullback_id] at h2
      convert h2 using 1
      ext V m
      simp [Sieve.pullback_apply, Presieve.functorPullback]

end CategoryTheory.Functor

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

namespace Thickening

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}

/-- **An object of `CRIS(X/S)` from a morphism of thickenings into an object of `CRIS(X/S)`.**
A divided power thickening `D` with a commuting square into the thickening of `A` becomes an
object of `CRIS(X/S)` by composing the structure maps of `A`. -/
def ofSquare (A : Thickening S) (D : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (t : D.target ⟶ A.thickening.target) (s : D.source ⟶ A.thickening.source)
    (hts : D.immersion ≫ t.hom = s ≫ A.thickening.immersion) : Thickening S where
  thickening := D
  toBase := t ≫ A.toBase
  toX := s ≫ A.toX
  over_base := by
    rw [DividedPowerScheme.Hom.comp_hom, ← Category.assoc, hts, Category.assoc, A.over_base,
      Category.assoc]

/-- The underlying thickening of `ofSquare A D t s hts` is `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofSquare_thickening (A : Thickening S) (D : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (t : D.target ⟶ A.thickening.target) (s : D.source ⟶ A.thickening.source)
    (hts : D.immersion ≫ t.hom = s ≫ A.thickening.immersion) :
    (ofSquare A D t s hts).thickening = D := rfl

/-- The map of `ofSquare A D t s hts` to the base is `t` followed by the map of `A` to the base.
-/
@[simp]
theorem ofSquare_toBase (A : Thickening S) (D : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (t : D.target ⟶ A.thickening.target) (s : D.source ⟶ A.thickening.source)
    (hts : D.immersion ≫ t.hom = s ≫ A.thickening.immersion) :
    (ofSquare A D t s hts).toBase = t ≫ A.toBase := rfl

/-- The map of `ofSquare A D t s hts` to `X` is `s` followed by the map of `A` to `X`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofSquare_toX (A : Thickening S) (D : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (t : D.target ⟶ A.thickening.target) (s : D.source ⟶ A.thickening.source)
    (hts : D.immersion ≫ t.hom = s ≫ A.thickening.immersion) :
    (ofSquare A D t s hts).toX = s ≫ A.toX := rfl

/-- The structure morphism of `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.ofSquare`, given
by the two maps of the square. -/
def ofSquareHom (A : Thickening S) (D : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (t : D.target ⟶ A.thickening.target) (s : D.source ⟶ A.thickening.source)
    (hts : D.immersion ≫ t.hom = s ≫ A.thickening.immersion) :
    ofSquare A D t s hts ⟶ A where
  sourceHom := s
  targetHom := t
  immersion_naturality := hts
  base_naturality := rfl
  toX_naturality := rfl

/-- The map of thickened schemes of `ofSquareHom A D t s hts` is `s`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofSquareHom_sourceHom (A : Thickening S) (D : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (t : D.target ⟶ A.thickening.target) (s : D.source ⟶ A.thickening.source)
    (hts : D.immersion ≫ t.hom = s ≫ A.thickening.immersion) :
    (ofSquareHom A D t s hts).sourceHom = s := rfl

/-- The map of ambient divided power schemes of `ofSquareHom A D t s hts` is `t`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofSquareHom_targetHom (A : Thickening S) (D : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (t : D.target ⟶ A.thickening.target) (s : D.source ⟶ A.thickening.source)
    (hts : D.immersion ≫ t.hom = s ≫ A.thickening.immersion) :
    (ofSquareHom A D t s hts).targetHom = t := rfl

/-- **The restriction of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to an open of its ambient scheme.**  The
underlying thickening is restricted to `V` and to its preimage in the thickened scheme, and the
structure maps are composed with the two open immersions. -/
noncomputable def restrictOpen (A : Thickening S) (V : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    Thickening S :=
  ofSquare A (A.thickening.restrict V) (A.thickening.target.restrictι V)
    (A.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι (morphismRestrict_ι A.thickening.immersion V)

/-- The underlying thickening of `A.restrictOpen V` is the restriction of that of `A` to `V`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictOpen_thickening (A : Thickening S) (V : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    (A.restrictOpen V).thickening = A.thickening.restrict V := rfl

/-- The structure morphism of `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.restrictOpen`,
given by the open immersion of `V` and the open immersion of its preimage. -/
noncomputable def restrictOpenHom (A : Thickening S) (V : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    A.restrictOpen V ⟶ A :=
  ofSquareHom A (A.thickening.restrict V) (A.thickening.target.restrictι V)
    (A.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι (morphismRestrict_ι A.thickening.immersion V)

/-- The map of thickened schemes of `A.restrictOpenHom V` is the open immersion of the preimage
of `V`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictOpenHom_sourceHom (A : Thickening S) (V : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    (A.restrictOpenHom V).sourceHom = (A.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι := rfl

/-- The map of ambient divided power schemes of `A.restrictOpenHom V` is the open immersion of
`V`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictOpenHom_targetHom (A : Thickening S) (V : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    (A.restrictOpenHom V).targetHom = A.thickening.target.restrictι V := rfl

/-- **The restriction of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to an open of its ambient scheme is
Cartesian.**  Restricting a morphism of schemes to the preimage of an open is a fibre square. -/
theorem isCartesian_restrictOpenHom (A : Thickening S)
    (V : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) : IsCartesian (A.restrictOpenHom V) :=
  (isPullback_morphismRestrict A.thickening.immersion V).flip

/-- The family of restrictions of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to a family of opens of its ambient
scheme. -/
noncomputable def restrictOpenCover (A : Thickening S) {ι : Type (u + 1)}
    (V : ι → A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} A where
  I₀ := ι
  X i := A.restrictOpen (V i)
  f i := A.restrictOpenHom (V i)

/-- **The restrictions of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to a family of opens covering its ambient
scheme form a Zariski covering family.**  Each member is Cartesian and the ambient scheme of the
member indexed by `i` is the open subscheme `V i`. -/
theorem isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover (A : Thickening S) {ι : Type (u + 1)}
    (V : ι → A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)
    (hV : ∀ x : A.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) :
    IsZariskiCovering (A.restrictOpenCover V) := by
  refine ⟨fun i ↦ A.isCartesian_restrictOpenHom (V i), ?_⟩
  change Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ (V i).toScheme) (fun i ↦ (V i).ι) ∈ _
  rw [Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff]
  refine ⟨fun x ↦ ?_, fun i ↦ inferInstance⟩
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hV x
  exact ⟨i, by simpa using hi⟩

section Cartesian

variable {B C : Thickening S} (q : B ⟶ C) [IsOpenImmersion q.targetHom.hom]

/-- **The divided power ideal of a Cartesian open immersion of `CRIS(X/S)` is the restriction of
the one below it**, on an affine open: the defining ideal of the thickened scheme of `B` over an
affine open `U` is the defining ideal of that of `C` over the image of `U`. -/
theorem appIso_inv_mem_ideal_of_isAffineOpen (hq : IsCartesian q)
    (U : B.thickening.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    {b : Γ(B.thickening.target.scheme, U.1)}
    (hb : b ∈ B.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op U.1)) :
    (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U.1).inv b ∈
      C.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U.1)) := by
  rw [B.thickening.ideal_eq_ker U,
    Scheme.ker_ideal_of_isPullback_of_isOpenImmersion
      C.thickening.immersion B.thickening.immersion q.sourceHom q.targetHom.hom hq.flip U] at hb
  rwa [C.thickening.ideal_eq_ker ⟨_, U.2.image_of_isOpenImmersion _⟩]

/-- **The divided power ideal of a Cartesian open immersion of `CRIS(X/S)` is the restriction of
the one below it.**  Membership in a quasi-coherent ideal subsheaf is local, so the affine case
suffices. -/
theorem appIso_inv_mem_ideal (hq : IsCartesian q) (U : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)
    {b : Γ(B.thickening.target.scheme, U)}
    (hb : b ∈ B.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op U)) :
    (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv b ∈
      C.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U)) := by
  refine C.thickening.target.ideal.isSheaf (X := op (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U)) _ ?_
  rintro _ ⟨y, hyU, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U₀, hU₀, rfl⟩, hyU₀, hU₀U⟩ :=
    B.thickening.target.scheme.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hyU U.2
  refine ⟨q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U₀, homOfLE (Set.image_mono hU₀U), ?_, ⟨y, hyU₀, rfl⟩⟩
  refine Set.mem_of_eq_of_mem ?_ (appIso_inv_mem_ideal_of_isAffineOpen q hq ⟨U₀, hU₀⟩
    (B.thickening.target.ideal.map_mem (homOfLE hU₀U).op hb))
  exact congrArg (fun φ : Γ(B.thickening.target.scheme, U) ⟶ _ ↦ φ.hom b)
    (Scheme.Hom.appIso_inv_naturality q.targetHom.hom ((homOfLE hU₀U).op)).symm

/-- **The comparison isomorphism on sections of a Cartesian open immersion of `CRIS(X/S)` is an
isomorphism of divided power rings.**  Its inverse carries the divided power ideal of `B` over an
open `U` into that of `C` over the image of `U`, and the divided powers agree because the
morphism is one of divided power schemes. -/
theorem isDPMorphism_appIso_inv (hq : IsCartesian q) (U : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism (B.thickening.target.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U))
      (C.thickening.target.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U)))
      (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv.hom := by
  have hinv : ∀ z, (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).hom.hom
      ((q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv.hom z) = z := (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv_hom_id_apply
  have hhom : ∀ z, (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv.hom
      ((q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).hom.hom z) = z := (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).hom_inv_id_apply
  have hφ : DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism
      (C.thickening.target.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U)))
      (B.thickening.target.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U))
      (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).hom.hom := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.appIso_hom]
    exact DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp _
      (B.thickening.target.dividedPowers.naturality
        (eqToHom (Scheme.Hom.preimage_image_eq q.targetHom.hom U).symm).op)
      (q.targetHom.compatible (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U))
  refine ⟨Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun x hx ↦ appIso_inv_mem_ideal q hq U hx,
    fun {n} a ha ↦ ?_⟩
  have h := hφ.dpow_comp (n := n) ((q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv.hom a)
    (appIso_inv_mem_ideal q hq U ha)
  have h' := (congrArg
    (fun w ↦ (B.thickening.target.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U)).dpow n w)
    (hinv a)).symm.trans h
  exact (hhom _).symm.trans
    (congrArg (fun w ↦ (q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv.hom w) h'.symm)

end Cartesian

section Lift

variable {B C D : Thickening S} (q : B ⟶ C) [IsOpenImmersion q.targetHom.hom] (r : D ⟶ C)

/-- The open of the ambient scheme of `D` whose points map into the image of the ambient scheme of
`B`; it is the largest open over which `r` factors through the open immersion `q`. -/
def pullbackOpen : D.thickening.target.scheme.Opens :=
  r.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ q.targetHom.hom.opensRange

/-- The image of `pullbackOpen q r` in the ambient scheme of `C` lies in the image of the ambient
scheme of `B`. -/
theorem range_comp_le_range_targetHom :
    Set.range ((pullbackOpen q r).ι ≫ r.targetHom.hom).base ⊆
      Set.range q.targetHom.hom.base := by
  rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
  exact x.2

/-- **The factorization of `r` through the open immersion `q` on ambient schemes**, over
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.pullbackOpen`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackLift :
    (pullbackOpen q r).toScheme ⟶ B.thickening.target.scheme :=
  IsOpenImmersion.lift q.targetHom.hom ((pullbackOpen q r).ι ≫ r.targetHom.hom)
    (range_comp_le_range_targetHom q r)

/-- The factorization `pullbackLift q r` followed by `q` is the restriction of `r` to
`pullbackOpen q r`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem pullbackLift_targetHom :
    pullbackLift q r ≫ q.targetHom.hom = (pullbackOpen q r).ι ≫ r.targetHom.hom :=
  IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac _ _ _

/-- The preimage of an open `U` under `pullbackLift q r` is the preimage under the restriction of
`r` of the image of `U` under `q`. -/
theorem pullbackLift_preimage (U : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    pullbackLift q r ⁻¹ᵁ U =
      (pullbackOpen q r).ι ⁻¹ᵁ (r.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U)) := by
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_preimage, ← pullbackLift_targetHom q r, Scheme.Hom.comp_preimage,
    Scheme.Hom.preimage_image_eq]

/-- The factorization on sections: the inverse of the comparison isomorphism of the open
immersion `q`, followed by the sections of `r` and a restriction. -/
theorem pullbackLift_app (U : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)
    (z : Γ(B.thickening.target.scheme, U)) :
    ((pullbackLift q r).app U).hom z =
      ((pullbackOpen q r).toScheme.presheaf.map
          (eqToHom (pullbackLift_preimage q r U)).op).hom
        (((pullbackOpen q r).ι.app (r.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U))).hom
          ((r.targetHom.hom.app (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U)).hom
            ((q.targetHom.hom.appIso U).inv.hom z))) :=
  congrArg (fun m : Γ(B.thickening.target.scheme, U) ⟶
      Γ((pullbackOpen q r).toScheme, pullbackLift q r ⁻¹ᵁ U) ↦ m.hom z)
    (IsOpenImmersion.lift_app q.targetHom.hom
      ((pullbackOpen q r).ι ≫ r.targetHom.hom) (range_comp_le_range_targetHom q r) U)

/-- **The factorization of `r` through `q` as a morphism of divided power schemes.**  Over an open
`U` of the ambient scheme of `B` the divided power ideal of `B` is the divided power ideal of `C`
over the image of `U`, so the factorization is compatible with the divided powers. -/
noncomputable def pullbackLiftTarget (hq : IsCartesian q) :
    D.thickening.target.restrict (pullbackOpen q r) ⟶ B.thickening.target where
  hom := pullbackLift q r
  compatible U := by
    have h := DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp _
      (DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp _
        (DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp _
          ((D.thickening.target.restrict (pullbackOpen q r)).dividedPowers.naturality
            (eqToHom (pullbackLift_preimage q r U)).op)
          ((D.thickening.target.restrictι (pullbackOpen q r)).compatible
            (r.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U))))
        (r.targetHom.compatible (q.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ U)))
      (isDPMorphism_appIso_inv q hq U)
    refine Eq.mpr (congrArg _ ?_) h
    exact RingHom.ext fun z ↦ pullbackLift_app q r U z

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of `pullbackLiftTarget q r hq` is `pullbackLift q r`. -/
@[simp]
theorem pullbackLiftTarget_hom (hq : IsCartesian q) :
    (pullbackLiftTarget q r hq).hom = pullbackLift q r := rfl

/-- The factorization `pullbackLiftTarget q r hq` followed by the map of ambient divided power
schemes of `q` is the restriction of that of `r` to `pullbackOpen q r`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem pullbackLiftTarget_targetHom (hq : IsCartesian q) :
    pullbackLiftTarget q r hq ≫ q.targetHom =
      D.thickening.target.restrictι (pullbackOpen q r) ≫ r.targetHom :=
  DividedPowerScheme.Hom.ext (pullbackLift_targetHom q r)

/-- The factorization of `r` through `q` on thickened schemes, obtained from the Cartesian square
of `q`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackLiftSource (hq : IsCartesian q) :
    (D.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ pullbackOpen q r).toScheme ⟶ B.thickening.source :=
  hq.lift ((D.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ pullbackOpen q r).ι ≫ r.sourceHom)
    (D.thickening.immersion ∣_ pullbackOpen q r ≫ pullbackLift q r) (by
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [pullbackLift_targetHom, morphismRestrict_ι_assoc, r.immersion_naturality])

/-- **The factorization of `r` through an open immersion `q` of `CRIS(X/S)`**, defined on the
restriction of `D` to the open of its ambient scheme over which the factorization exists. -/
noncomputable def pullbackLiftHom (hq : IsCartesian q) :
    D.restrictOpen (pullbackOpen q r) ⟶ B where
  sourceHom := pullbackLiftSource q r hq
  targetHom := pullbackLiftTarget q r hq
  immersion_naturality := (hq.lift_snd _ _ _).symm
  base_naturality :=
    calc pullbackLiftTarget q r hq ≫ B.toBase
        = pullbackLiftTarget q r hq ≫ q.targetHom ≫ C.toBase := by rw [q.base_naturality]
      _ = (pullbackLiftTarget q r hq ≫ q.targetHom) ≫ C.toBase := (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
      _ = (D.thickening.target.restrictι (pullbackOpen q r) ≫ r.targetHom) ≫ C.toBase := by
            rw [pullbackLiftTarget_targetHom]
      _ = D.thickening.target.restrictι (pullbackOpen q r) ≫ D.toBase := by
            rw [Category.assoc, r.base_naturality]
  toX_naturality :=
    calc pullbackLiftSource q r hq ≫ B.toX
        = pullbackLiftSource q r hq ≫ q.sourceHom ≫ C.toX := by rw [q.toX_naturality]
      _ = (pullbackLiftSource q r hq ≫ q.sourceHom) ≫ C.toX := (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
      _ = ((D.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ pullbackOpen q r).ι ≫ r.sourceHom) ≫ C.toX := by
            rw [show pullbackLiftSource q r hq ≫ q.sourceHom = _ from hq.lift_fst _ _ _]
      _ = (D.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ pullbackOpen q r).ι ≫ D.toX := by
            rw [Category.assoc, r.toX_naturality]

/-- The factorization `pullbackLiftHom q r hq` followed by `q` is the restriction of `r` to
`pullbackOpen q r`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem pullbackLiftHom_comp (hq : IsCartesian q) :
    pullbackLiftHom q r hq ≫ q = D.restrictOpenHom (pullbackOpen q r) ≫ r :=
  Hom.ext (hq.lift_fst _ _ _) (pullbackLiftTarget_targetHom q r hq)

end Lift

end Thickening

variable {S S' : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} {f : S.S ⟶ S'.S} {g : S.X ⟶ S'.X}
  {h : S.toClosedFiber ≫ DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberMap f = g ≫ S'.toClosedFiber}

/-- **Change of divided power base.**  A divided power thickening of `X` relative to `(S, I, γ)`
is one of `Y` relative to `(S', I', γ')`, with structure maps `T ⟶ S ⟶ S'` and `U ⟶ X ⟶ Y`.  The
underlying thickening and the maps between thickenings are unchanged. -/
@[stacks 07IC "the functor"]
noncomputable def changeBase (S S' : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) (f : S.S ⟶ S'.S)
    (g : S.X ⟶ S'.X)
    (h : S.toClosedFiber ≫ DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberMap f = g ≫ S'.toClosedFiber) :
    Thickening S ⥤ Thickening S' where
  obj A :=
    { thickening := A.thickening
      toBase := A.toBase ≫ f
      toX := A.toX ≫ g
      over_base := by
        calc A.thickening.immersion ≫ (A.toBase ≫ f).hom
            = (A.thickening.immersion ≫ A.toBase.hom) ≫ f.hom := by
              simp [DividedPowerScheme.Hom.comp_hom]
          _ = (A.toX ≫ sourceToBase S) ≫ f.hom := by rw [A.over_base]
          _ = A.toX ≫ (S.toClosedFiber ≫ DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberMap f) ≫
                DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberι S'.S := by simp [sourceToBase]
          _ = (A.toX ≫ g) ≫ sourceToBase S' := by rw [h]; simp [sourceToBase] }
  map {A B} k :=
    { sourceHom := k.sourceHom
      targetHom := k.targetHom
      immersion_naturality := k.immersion_naturality
      base_naturality := by
        change k.targetHom ≫ (B.toBase ≫ f) = A.toBase ≫ f
        rw [← Category.assoc, k.base_naturality]
      toX_naturality := by
        change k.sourceHom ≫ (B.toX ≫ g) = A.toX ≫ g
        rw [← Category.assoc, k.toX_naturality] }
  map_id A := by apply Thickening.Hom.ext <;> rfl
  map_comp k l := by apply Thickening.Hom.ext <;> rfl

/-- Change of base does not change the underlying thickening of an object. -/
@[simp]
theorem changeBase_obj_thickening (A : Thickening S) :
    ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A).thickening = A.thickening := rfl

/-- The map to the base of the image of `A` under change of base is that of `A` followed by `f`.
-/
@[simp]
theorem changeBase_obj_toBase (A : Thickening S) :
    ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A).toBase = A.toBase ≫ f := rfl

/-- The map to `Y` of the image of `A` under change of base is that of `A` to `X` followed by `g`.
-/
@[simp]
theorem changeBase_obj_toX (A : Thickening S) :
    ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A).toX = A.toX ≫ g := rfl

/-- Change of base does not change the map of thickened schemes of a morphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem changeBase_map_sourceHom {A B : Thickening S} (k : A ⟶ B) :
    ((changeBase S S' f g h).map k).sourceHom = k.sourceHom := rfl

/-- Change of base does not change the map of ambient divided power schemes of a morphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem changeBase_map_targetHom {A B : Thickening S} (k : A ⟶ B) :
    ((changeBase S S' f g h).map k).targetHom = k.targetHom := rfl

namespace Thickening

/-- **The comparison morphism of a rebased object.**  An object `B` of `CRIS(Y/S')` over the
image of `A` is, as a divided power thickening, an object of `CRIS(X/S)` over `A`; the identity
of the underlying thickening identifies the image of the latter with `B`. -/
noncomputable def ofSquareComparison {A : Thickening S} {B : Thickening S'}
    (k : B ⟶ (changeBase S S' f g h).obj A) :
    (changeBase S S' f g h).obj
        (ofSquare A B.thickening k.targetHom k.sourceHom k.immersion_naturality) ⟶ B where
  sourceHom := 𝟙 B.thickening.source
  targetHom := 𝟙 B.thickening.target
  immersion_naturality := (Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm
  base_naturality :=
    (Category.id_comp _).trans (k.base_naturality.symm.trans (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm)
  toX_naturality :=
    (Category.id_comp _).trans (k.toX_naturality.symm.trans (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm)

/-- The structure morphism of a rebased object maps to the original morphism, up to the
comparison isomorphism of the underlying thickenings. -/
theorem changeBase_map_ofSquareHom {A : Thickening S} {B : Thickening S'}
    (k : B ⟶ (changeBase S S' f g h).obj A) :
    (changeBase S S' f g h).map
        (ofSquareHom A B.thickening k.targetHom k.sourceHom k.immersion_naturality) =
      ofSquareComparison k ≫ k :=
  Hom.ext (Category.id_comp _).symm (Category.id_comp _).symm

/-- **A family of morphisms into the image of `A`, read as a family of morphisms into `A`.**
Change of base leaves the underlying thickenings and the maps between them untouched, so each
member of the family is already a divided power thickening over that of `A`. -/
noncomputable def rebase {A : Thickening S}
    (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A)) :
    PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} A where
  I₀ := E.I₀
  X i := ofSquare A (E.X i).thickening (E.f i).targetHom (E.f i).sourceHom
    (E.f i).immersion_naturality
  f i := ofSquareHom A (E.X i).thickening (E.f i).targetHom (E.f i).sourceHom
    (E.f i).immersion_naturality

/-- **A Zariski covering family of the image of `A` rebases to a Zariski covering family of
`A`.**  Both conditions — that the squares be Cartesian and that the ambient schemes form a
Zariski covering — only involve data that change of base preserves. -/
theorem isZariskiCovering_rebase {A : Thickening S}
    (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A))
    (hE : IsZariskiCovering E) : IsZariskiCovering (rebase E) :=
  ⟨hE.1, hE.2⟩

/-- The sieve generated by a rebased family is contained in the pullback along change of base of
the sieve generated by the original family. -/
theorem generate_rebase_le {A : Thickening S}
    (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A)) :
    Sieve.generate (rebase E).presieve₀ ≤
      Sieve.functorPullback (changeBase S S' f g h) (Sieve.generate E.presieve₀) := by
  rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff]
  rintro W q ⟨i⟩
  exact ⟨E.X i, ofSquareComparison (E.f i), E.f i, ⟨i⟩,
    (changeBase_map_ofSquareHom (E.f i)).symm⟩

end Thickening

open Thickening

/-- **Cover lifting for change of base, for a covering sieve refined by a Zariski covering
family.**  If a sieve on the image of `A` contains a Zariski covering family, then its pullback
along change of base is a covering sieve of `A` in the big crystalline site of `X/S`. -/
theorem changeBase_functorPullback_mem_topology {A : Thickening S}
    {T : Sieve ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A)}
    (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A))
    (hE : IsZariskiCovering E) (hET : E.presieve₀ ≤ T.arrows) :
    Sieve.functorPullback (changeBase S S' f g h) T ∈ topology S A := by
  refine (topology S).superset_covering ?_
    (zariskiCovering_mem_topology S (rebase E) (isZariskiCovering_rebase E hE))
  exact (generate_rebase_le E).trans
    (Sieve.functorPullback_monotone _ A ((Sieve.generate_le_iff _ _).2 hET))

/-- **Cover lifting for change of base, for the sieve generated by a Zariski covering family.**
The sieve generated by a Zariski covering family of the image of `A` pulls back along change of
base to a covering sieve of `A` in the big crystalline site of `X/S`. -/
theorem changeBase_functorPullback_generate_mem_topology {A : Thickening S}
    (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} ((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A))
    (hE : IsZariskiCovering E) :
    Sieve.functorPullback (changeBase S S' f g h) (Sieve.generate E.presieve₀) ∈
      topology S A :=
  changeBase_functorPullback_mem_topology E hE (Sieve.le_generate _)

/-- **Cover lifting for change of base.**  Let `{(Uᵢ, Tᵢ, δᵢ) ⟶ B}` be a Zariski covering family
in `CRIS(Y/S')` and let `p` be a morphism from the image of `A` to `B`.  The restrictions of `A`
to the opens `p⁻¹(Tᵢ)` of its ambient scheme form a Zariski covering family of the image of `A`,
and each member factors through `(Uᵢ, Tᵢ, δᵢ)`; so the pullback along `p` of the sieve generated
by the family pulls back along change of base to a covering sieve of `A`. -/
theorem changeBase_functorPullback_pullback_mem_topology {A : Thickening S} {X : Thickening S'}
    (p : (changeBase S S' f g h).obj A ⟶ X) (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X)
    (hE : IsZariskiCovering E) :
    Sieve.functorPullback (changeBase S S' f g h)
      ((Sieve.generate E.presieve₀).pullback p) ∈ topology S A := by
  have hE' : (∀ x, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range ((E.f i).targetHom.hom).base) ∧
      ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion (E.f i).targetHom.hom := by
    simpa [targetPresieve] using hE.2
  refine changeBase_functorPullback_mem_topology
    (((changeBase S S' f g h).obj A).restrictOpenCover
      (fun i ↦ have := hE'.2 i; pullbackOpen (E.f i) p)) ?_ ?_
  · exact isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover _ _ fun x ↦ hE'.1 (p.targetHom.hom x)
  · rintro W m ⟨i⟩
    have := hE'.2 i
    exact ⟨E.X i, pullbackLiftHom (E.f i) p (hE.1 i), E.f i, ⟨i⟩,
      pullbackLiftHom_comp (E.f i) p (hE.1 i)⟩

/-- Change of divided power base is cocontinuous for the big
crystalline Zariski topologies. -/
@[stacks 07IC "cocontinuity"]
instance changeBase_isCocontinuous :
    (changeBase S S' f g h).IsCocontinuous (topology S) (topology S') :=
  Functor.isCocontinuous_toGrothendieck _ _ _ fun A _ p R hR ↦ by
    obtain ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩ := hR
    exact changeBase_functorPullback_pullback_mem_topology p E hE

/-- The morphism of crystalline topoi
`(X/S)_CRIS ⟶ (Y/S')_CRIS` induced by change of divided power base: its pushforward is the sheaf
pushforward along the cocontinuous functor `changeBase`, and its inverse image is the sheaf
pullback, which is left exact. -/
@[stacks 07IC "the morphism of topoi", sga "4 III 2.3" "special case"]
noncomputable def changeBaseMorphism (S S' : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) (f : S.S ⟶ S'.S)
    (g : S.X ⟶ S'.X)
    (h : S.toClosedFiber ≫ DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberMap f = g ≫ S'.toClosedFiber) :
    MorphismOfTopoi (topos S) (topos S') where
  pushforward := (changeBase S S' f g h).sheafPushforwardCocontinuous
    (Type (u + 1)) (topology S) (topology S')
  inverseImage := (changeBase S S' f g h).sheafPullbackCocontinuous
    (Type (u + 1)) (topology S) (topology S')
  adj := (changeBase S S' f g h).sheafAdjunctionPullbackCocontinuous
    (Type (u + 1)) (topology S) (topology S')
  preservesFiniteLimits := inferInstance

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

end
